+## 4.1.21 (HexGhoul): katana cuts with wrists, the hands always in front of you
+
+HexKagune 4.1.21 for Forge 1.20.1. Not tested in game. Previews: `docs/handoff/katana-cuts-4.1.21.png` (every cut from the front, the side,
+behind and above), `docs/handoff/katana-cuts-before-after-4.1.21.png` (your frames, before and after).
+
+Your words, of the katana's cuts: "Why the fuck is the sword behind the fucking back? That, like, both arms are reaching behind the player's
+back. What is that?"
+
+**What it was:** the katana was welded to the forearm at one angle, its chudan angle. To point the blade down and to the left (the end of
+a kesa-giri), the only arm angle that does that swings the arm up and back. The solver behind the cuts (4.1.18) cared about the blade's
+direction far more than where the hands were, so in kesa-giri's follow-through, gyaku-kesa's wind-up and yoko-giri's follow-through both
+hands went behind your back, through your body. It also asked for hand positions no straight arm can reach, and at rest in chudan the
+left fist sat a pixel inside your stomach with the hilt through it. Nothing checked any of this.
+
+**Now:**
+
+- **Wrists.** The katana turns in your grip the way a swordsman's wrists cock at the end of a cut, up to a real wrist's reach. Your hands
+  stay in front of you while the blade points down and away.
+- **Every cut re-solved** where straight arms can actually reach: kesa-giri rises into jodan before your face and cuts down across to the
+  left, gyaku-kesa rises from low left to high right, yoko-giri lays the blade out right and sweeps it flat across, the tsuki drives
+  straight out on a lunge, and the spinning finisher stays as it was. Each blade path and body motion is the same as before; only the hands
+  moved to where they can be.
+- **Chudan** is a firm, high guard: the blade at an opponent's head, both hands a fist in front of your chest.
+- **The hilt** now ends just past your left hand, with the pommel in the heel of the hand, as a katana is held. The guard is a katana's size.
+- Drawn the same way for you (third and first person) and for every investigator holding one.
+- **Checked:**
+  - At every 2% of every cut, both fists are in front of you or beside you, never behind.
+  - The blade, guard, hilt and both arms never go into your torso, head or legs.
+  - The wrists stay within a wrist's reach.
+  - The weapon drawn by the renderer turns exactly as the arm says.
+
+**Not yet:** the other quinques still swing the old way. Each one gets this treatment, a string of its own and a kagune mesh, one at a
+time, starting with the mace (its second swing winds up behind the head).
+
+### Other
+
+- Protocol 117 (unchanged).
